<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Holstein-Gottorp</h1><p class="st-meta">1544 CE – 1773 CE · capital Schleswig</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The ducal branch of the Danish royal house that shared Schleswig and Holstein with the kings and later produced the tsars of Russia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1544 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-iii-of-denmark">Christian III of Denmark</a> divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> with his half-brothers. Adolf received the Gottorp share, ruled from Gottorp castle at Schleswig, founding the house of Holstein-Gottorp; its lands lay intermingled with the royal parts of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-schleswig">Duchy of Schleswig</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-holstein">Duchy of Holstein</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes kept a splendid Lutheran court at Gottorp, where Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-duke-of-holstein-gottorp">Frederick III</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrichstadt">Friedrichstadt</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/remonstrants">Remonstrants</a> and sponsored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adam-olearius">Adam Olearius's</a> embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and the great Gottorp globe. Allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, they won full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over their part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> in 1658, only to lose it in the Great Northern War.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> seized the Gottorp lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> in 1713, a loss confirmed in 1720. Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-duke-of-holstein-gottorp">Charles Frederick</a>'s son became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-russia">Peter III of Russia</a>, and in 1773 Peter's son Paul exchanged the Gottorp part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> with Denmark for <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-oldenburg">Oldenburg</a>, ending the duchy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-holstein-gottorp.jpg" alt="Duchy of Holstein-Gottorp" width="320" height="403"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_Dynastie_Holstein-Gottorp.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1544 CE – 1773 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Schleswig</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Adolf, Frederick III, Charles Frederick</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/denmark">Denmark</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Schleswig-Holstein-Gottorp, Gottorp, Holstein-Gottorp</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1658&amp;focus=duchy-of-holstein-gottorp" aria-label="Duchy of Holstein-Gottorp on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4891 311 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Holstein-Gottorp lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5211 567L5209 586M5211 567L5381 440M5211 567L5274 535M5211 567L5229 694M5211 567L6487 457M5211 567L5274 535"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5209 586h0M5381 440h0M5274 535h0M5229 694h0M6487 457h0M5274 535h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5211 567h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5211 567h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Schleswig. <a href="/atlas?year=1658&amp;focus=duchy-of-holstein-gottorp">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
